      "title": "Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator",
      "description": "Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Home Jobs Mission/Values DEI Benefits Applicant Login Kiosk mode Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 12 Month Faculty Opening at: Sep 3 2026 - 09:00 CDT Add to favorites View favorites VP Area: Nursing School Department: Nursing School FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: The Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Kramer School of Nursing and serves as the designated Nurse Administrator for purposes of ACEN accreditation and Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions, the Senior Associate Dean holds the authority and accountability required of the Nurse Administrator under Oklahoma Board of Nursing rules, including direct responsibility for administration of the School’s nursing education program, preparation and administration of the School budget, implementation of faculty development programs, and recommendation of qualified faculty for appointment, promotion, tenure (if applicable), and retention. The Senior Associate Dean ensures compliance and alignment with applicable accreditation and regulatory body standards and reporting requirements. As a senior member of college leadership, the Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator works collaboratively with the Dean in providing strategic and operational direction for the College. To learn more: Senior Associate Dean Nurse Administrator Prospectus (Aug 2026).pdf Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree required; degree must be in nursing, or a related field with a Master of Science in Nursing also held. Evidence of current practice with a minimum of five (5) years full-time equivalent practice as a Registered Nurse in a clinical setting, preceding the first date of employment as faculty per requirements of the Oklahoma Nursing Practice Act and Rules and Regulations of said Act. 485:10-5-3.2 (2024) Minimum of five (5) years teaching experience at the baccalaureate level or higher in nursing Demonstrated knowledge of nursing accreditation standards (ACEN or CCNE) and Oklahoma Board of Nursing requirements Hold a valid license to practice as a Registered Nurse in the State of Oklahoma (or receive licensure before start date) Preferred Qualifications: Academic administrative experience preferred Job Duties: Academic and Program Leadership Oversees the academic programs of the Kramer School of Nursing, ensuring compliance with requirements of the Board of Trustees, the President, and applicable accreditation bodies, and keeping the Dean informed of program status and significant developments. Supports continuous improvement of nursing education programs by contributing to the assessment, planning, implementation, and evaluation of School programs under the Dean's direction. Assures that adequate provisions are made to advise nursing students regarding their academic programs. Oversees the day-to-day quality of instruction and availability of academic resources. Teaches courses as assigned based on programmatic and operational needs. Retains nursing expertise through continued education and practice. Administrative and Operational Leadership Holds primary responsibility for preparation and administration of the KSN budget with faculty input; monitors expenditures and ensures fiscal operations align with the allocation framework established in coordination with the Dean. Supports the Dean in organizing the School to efficiently administer its academic and administrative programs and committees. Administers the Office of the Senior Associate Dean in a manner that fosters responsiveness to students, faculty, senior university management, and other university offices, in alignment with the Dean's direction. Directs faculty development and evaluation processes; makes recommendations to the Dean regarding promotion, tenure, and retention; and oversees faculty workload and overload policies consistent with accreditation standards and OBN requirements. Assists with schedule development and faculty teaching assignments, subject to Dean approval. Supports recruitment, hiring, and orientation of faculty and staff for the School in coordination with the Dean, assuring that qualifications meet professional accreditation standards. Monitors School faculty and staff capacity and brings workforce needs to the Dean's attention. Manages staff time records and leave requests as assigned. Coordinates financial aid awarded by the School as directed by the Dean and university policy. Accreditation and Compliance Serves as the designated Nurse Administrator and primary institutional authority on nursing accreditation, bringing specialized expertise in ACEN or CCNE standards. Leads all accreditation activities for the KSN, including self-study preparation, site visit coordination, and ongoing compliance with ACEN or CCNE standards and Oklahoma Board of Nursing approval requirements. Keeps the Dean informed of accreditation status, findings, and required actions, translating nursing-specific accreditation requirements into institutional context. Directs program assessment processes to ensure continuous quality improvement in alignment with accreditation standards. Responsible for notification to the Oklahoma Board of Nursing of faculty appointments, changes in the program or its administration, and reports as directed by the Board. Adheres to all policies within the Oklahoma City University Faculty Handbook and the KSN Employee Handbook. Strategic Planning and University Engagement Contributes to the strategic planning processes of the School and the College of Nursing and Health Professions under the Dean's leadership. Supports the School executive board and serves as a liaison between the School, the university, and the broader nursing community, as directed by the Dean. Maintains collaborative working relationships with other academic and administrative offices on campus on behalf of the School. Participates in university-wide activities and committees as appropriate or as directed by the Dean or university senior leadership. Serves as representative to nursing education and service organizations as designated by the Dean. External Relations and Scholarship Represents the School in local, state, national, and international settings through public speaking and other roles, as authorized by the Dean. Supports fundraising efforts for the School in coordination with and under the direction of the Dean. Participates in externally validated scholarly activities and professional organizations as both member and leader. Serves as a resource in areas of expertise to faculty, personnel, and the community. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to speak effectively before both large and small groups Ability to engage with diverse constituencies with multiple and competing interests Excellent writing skills, as demonstrated in professional work samples submitted with application materials Excellent interpersonal and oral communication skills Commitment to diversity among School personnel and a cross-cultural curriculum Proficiency in word processing, spreadsheet, and presentation software Excellent problem-solving, leadership, and management skills Ability to understand and balance both faculty and student perspectives Strong work ethic, personal integrity, and positive outlook on challenges Detail-oriented, organized, and punctual in managing work and personnel Commitment to upholding the mission of Oklahoma City University Physical Demands and Working Conditions: Constantly operates a computer and other office machinery. Constantly visually identifies, observes, and assesses. Frequently communicates with university constituents. Frequently remains in a stationary position (standing and/or sitting). Occasionally moves to accomplish tasks and/or to get from one worksite to another. Occasionally moves common office materials. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations (in accordance with ADA requirements) may be made, upon request, to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work is primarily indoors, with some travel between campus buildings or off campus Attendance at evening and weekend events may be required Off-campus, state, regional, and national travel may be required Exposure to frequent noise caused by telephones and office machines Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert cfdd56f9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Nursing School Nursing School Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 718ddb19 Last Name (required) 8cea60c1 Email (required) beeacfec Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director of Academic Achievement Law School Oklahoma City University School of Law seeks a Director of Academic Achievement, to begin on August 1, 2027.  This may be either a staff or faculty position, as described below. Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator Nursing School The Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Kramer School of Nursing and serves as the designated Nurse Administrator for purposes of ACEN accreditation and Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions, the Senior Associate Dean holds the authority and accountability required of the Nurse Administrator under Oklahoma Board of Nursing rules, including direct responsibility for administration of the School’s nursing education program, preparation and administration of the School budget, implementation of faculty development programs, and recommendation of qualified faculty for appointment, promotion, tenure (if applicable), and retention. The Senior Associate Dean ensures compliance and alignment with applicable accreditation and regulatory body standards and reporting requirements. As a senior member of college leadership, the Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator works collaboratively with the Dean in providing strategic and operational direction for the College. Program Director Law School OKLAHOMA CITY UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applications for the position of Program Director for the launch of its online J.D. program, which is currently being developed.   The online J.D. program will be fully online, and courses are likely to be both asynchronous and synchronous.  All online J.D. program faculty and staff will fulfill their responsibilities in person at OCU Law. Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing School The Kramer School of Nursing at Oklahoma City University invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure track Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing position. The successful candidate will begin as soon as possible. Recruitment Specialist Human Resources Oklahoma City University is seeking an organized, service-minded Recruitment Specialist to coordinate hiring across our campus community, from the first job posting to the new hire's first day. This role is ideal for an HR professional who thrives on process, is ready for ownership of a function, and understands that every search reflects the institution. Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist Facilities This position is responsible for the day-to-day maintenance operations of the HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and mechanical systems for the university. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 8e3d02fb Last Name (required) d6b1d6fc Email (required) 382d93bf Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Employment Opportunity Oklahoma City University pledges to recruit, select, and promote diversity by providing equality of opportunity in higher education for all current and prospective students, faculty, and staff with respect to hiring, continuation, promotion and tenure, and applications for admission or employment, without discrimination or segregation based on sex (gender), race, age, ancestry, color, disability, genetic history, national origin, marital status, medical condition, religious creed, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, pregnancy, parenting status, status as a veteran, or the perception that a person has one or more of these characteristics. For questions, concerns, and/or additional information, please contact: Applicants/Employees (ADA/Section 504) – Office of Human Resources: chamilton@okcu.edu / 405-208-6330 Title IX – Vice President for Student Affairs (Title IX Coordinator): aayres@okcu.edu / 405.208.7900 Titles VI and VII, Section 504 Title III, ADA and amendments, and ADEA – Chief Human Resources Officer: bbenson@okcu.edu / 405.208.6020 About Us | Contact Us Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Oklahoma City University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
