    "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/recruitment-specialist-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Recruitment Specialist",
      "description": "Recruitment Specialist - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Home Jobs Mission/Values DEI Benefits Applicant Login Kiosk mode Recruitment Specialist Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Administration Regular Full-Time Staff Opening at: Aug 31 2026 - 09:00 CDT Add to favorites View favorites VP Area: Human Resources Department: Human Resources FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: Full-Time | | $20.67 – $22.84/hour Oklahoma City University is seeking an organized, service-minded Recruitment Specialist to coordinate hiring across our campus community, from the first job posting to the new hire's first day. This role is ideal for an HR professional who thrives on process, is ready for ownership of a function, and understands that every search reflects the institution. What You'll Do Coordinate searches across all employment types, staff, faculty, adjunct, and contingent, from vacancy approval through offer acceptance Work with hiring managers to develop search strategies, build interview processes, and keep things moving Own and operate our applicant tracking system (PageUp), including training others and keeping data clean Be the point of contact candidates hear from first and count on through pre-boarding: offer, background check, I-9, and Banner record setup Train hiring managers on process and procedure so searches run consistently and every candidate is treated with respect, including the ones we don't hire Expand how we recruit: job fairs, sourcing strategies, employer brand, community partnerships Track what's working, flag what isn't, and bring ideas Contribute to the department's ongoing efforts to enhance employee engagement and recognition across the university community What You'll Bring 3+ years of progressive HR, talent acquisition, or related experience Strong organizational skills and genuine attention to detail Experience with applicant tracking systems or complex HR software A service orientation, responsive, organized, and welcoming whether you're talking to a finalist or a frustrated hiring manager The instinct to ask questions and the confidence to raise a concern when something doesn't seem right Associate's degree required; bachelor's preferred. Relevant experience may substitute year for year. PHR or SHRM-CP a plus, we'll support you in getting there. Higher education experience and PageUp or Banner familiarity are a bonus, not a requirement. Why You'll Want to Work Here You'll join a small, collaborative HR team that works closely with leaders and employees across the university to support great hires, smooth onboarding, and a positive employee experience. Health & Wellness Choice of medical plans with OCU covering 70% of employee premiums On-campus health clinic at no cost to plan members $0 telehealth for medical and behavioral health Dental, vision, prescription savings, and free campus fitness center access Weekly paid wellness time Time Off That Matters Generous PTO including vacation, sick leave, and ~16.5 paid holidays Summer schedule with Fridays off, full pay, four-day workweek Financial Security 403(b) retirement plan with up to 5% university match Employer-paid basic life insurance and long-term disability FSA and HSA options with university HSA matching Education & Campus Perks Tuition remission for employees and eligible dependents National tuition exchange program participation Free admission to athletic events, discounted arts performances and meals Employee Assistance Program Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ed9d8942 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Human Resources Human Resources Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United St