    "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/adult-gerontology-acute-care-nurse-practitioner-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner",
      "description": "Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Home Jobs Mission/Values DEI Benefits Applicant Login Kiosk mode Adult-Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 9 Month Faculty Opening at: Aug 31 2026 - 09:00 CDT Add to favorites View favorites VP Area: Nursing School Department: Nursing School FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: Kramer School of Nursing invites applicants for a full-time or half-time adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner (AGACNP) beginning January 2027. The NP Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor position is a non-tenure track, nine-month appointment renewable annually based on performance and need.  Faculty rank will be assigned based on incumbent qualifications: Clinical Instructors meet minimum qualifications; Assistant Professors hold a doctorate. The faculty member will: Prepare and conduct courses in conformity with outcomes of the university, Kramer School of Nursing, and approving accrediting agencies Evaluate student learning, skills, and abilities; and maintain records of such evaluations Engagement in scholarship that supports Kramer School of Nursing’s mission Serve the University and the Kramer School of Nursing, including committee work as appropriate Participate in professional organizations as a member Adhere to all policies within the Oklahoma City University Faculty Handbook, KSN Employee Handbook, the OCU Student Handbook, and the KSN Student Handbook Participation in the OCU assessment program, and in student recruiting and retention efforts for KSN and the university Other duties as assigned. Education and Experience: Education: Terminal degree preferred Oklahoma RN with APRN recognition required MSN or DNP degree, Adult Gero Acute Care NP certification required Preference will be given to candidates who hold dual national certification as a nurse practitioner, including AGACNP certification Experience: Evidence of current practice with a minimum of two years full-time equivalent practice as a Registered Nurse in a clinical setting preceding the first date of first employment as a teacher.* Two (2) years of advanced practice nursing experience required. Both clinical and teaching experience are preferred, but related professional credentials will be considered. *per requirements of the Oklahoma Nursing Practice Act and Rules and Regulations of said Act. (1994) Additional Qualifications: Valid license to practice as a registered nurse and nurse practitioner in Oklahoma National certification as an adult-gerontology acute care nurse practitioner Kramer School of Nursing: Established in 1981, Kramer School of Nursing is now the premier private nursing school in the seven-state region in all quality measures. The School is committed to providing educational and service opportunities that prepare professional nurses who practice with integrity, knowledge, and compassion. In addition to the pre-licensure baccalaureate program offered in part-time, full-time, and accelerated options to first and second bachelor’s degree students, Kramer also offers the RN-to-BSN (both on campus and in rural areas), the Master of Science in Nursing,  the Doctor of Nursing Practice (including the Family Nurse Practitioner, Adult Gerontology Acute Care Nurse Practitioner, and Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner). The University: Oklahoma City University was founded in 1904 and is a coeducational, urban, private university located in the Uptown district of Oklahoma City. The university is affiliated with the United Methodist Church and offers a wide variety of degrees in the liberal arts and sciences disciplines. Oklahoma City University is the only Oklahoma institution listed in the top tier of the regional, master's-level university category by U.S. News and World Report magazine. Required Application Materials All applications submitted must include: CV and Cover Letter with Professional References listed Statement of Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 829b6889 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Nursing School Nursing School Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) b0a604de Last Name (required) 03916e78 Email (required) 13e0f876 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director of Academic Achievement Law School Oklahoma City University School of Law seeks a Director of Academic Achievement, to begin on August 1, 2027.  This may be either a staff or faculty position, as described below. Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator Nursing School The Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Kramer School of Nursing and serves as the designated Nurse Administrator for purposes of ACEN accreditation and Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions, the Senior Associate Dean holds the authority and accountability required of the Nurse Administrator under Oklahoma Board of Nursing rules, including direct responsibility for administration of the School’s nursing education program, preparation and administration of the School budget, implementation of faculty development programs, and recommendation of qualified faculty for appointment, promotion, tenure (if applicable), and retention. The Senior Associate Dean ensures compliance and alignment with applicable accreditation and regulatory body standards and reporting requirements. As a senior member of college leadership, the Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator works collaboratively with the Dean in providing strategic and operational direction for the College. Program Director Law School OKLAHOMA CITY UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applications for the position of Program Director for the launch of its online J.D. program, which is currently being developed.   The online J.D. program will be fully online, and courses are likely to be both asynchronous and synchronous.  All online J.D. program faculty and staff will fulfill their responsibilities in person at OCU Law. Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing School The Kramer School of Nursing at Oklahoma City University invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure track Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing position. The successful candidate will begin as soon as possible. Recruitment Specialist Human Resources Oklahoma City University is seeking an organized, service-minded Recruitment Specialist to coordinate hiring across our campus community, from the first job posting to the new hire's first day. This role is ideal for an HR professional who thrives on process, is ready for ownership of a function, and understands that every search reflects the institution. Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist Facilities This position is responsible for the day-to-day maintenance operations of the HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and mechanical systems for the university. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4c9be04d Last Name (required) 688d688b Email (required) 635aacb0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Employment Opportunity Oklahoma City University pledges to recruit, select, and promote diversity by providing equality of opportunity in higher education for all current and prospective students, faculty, and staff with respect to hiring, continuation, promotion and tenure, and applications for admission or employment, without discrimi