    "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/hvac-maintenance-technician-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "HVAC Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "HVAC Maintenance Technician - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Home Jobs Mission/Values DEI Benefits Applicant Login Kiosk mode HVAC Maintenance Technician Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Facilities Regular Full-Time Staff Opening at: Aug 21 2026 - 09:00 CDT Add to favorites View favorites VP Area: Facilities Department: Facilities FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Hourly rate: $17.30 Position Summary: Oklahoma City University is hiring two HVAC Maintenance Technicians! Are you an experienced HVAC professional who enjoys hands-on work, troubleshooting, and solving problems? Join a team where your skills make a difference every day. As an HVAC Maintenance Technician at OCU, you'll help keep our campus buildings, classrooms, offices, and facilities comfortable, safe, and operating efficiently. You'll work with a variety of HVAC, refrigeration, plumbing, and mechanical systems while collaborating with experienced Facilities professionals. Whether you're looking to build on your current experience or expand your technical skills, you'll have the opportunity to learn, contribute, and grow. What You'll Do In this role, you'll: Repair, maintain, and assist with the installation of HVAC systems, refrigerators, freezers, plumbing systems, appliances, and other campus equipment. Perform preventive maintenance and troubleshoot mechanical and electromechanical systems. Assist with inspecting and testing air conditioning and refrigeration equipment to ensure proper operation and efficiency. Test and adjust thermostatic controls, blowers, refrigerant systems, and other HVAC components. Assist with maintaining accurate records related to equipment repairs, preventive maintenance, and refrigerant/chemical use. Install, repair, and renovate plumbing and HVAC systems as needed. Read and interpret blueprints, block diagrams, electrical schematics, and ladder diagrams. Work with components such as motors, bearings, pumps, compressors, starters, couplings, sheaves, pneumatic systems, and air-handling equipment. Respond to daily work orders and provide general Facilities maintenance support across campus. Follow required safety procedures, including lockout/tagout, chemical safety, PPE, hazard communication, lifting procedures, and fire safety. Work collaboratively with Facilities team members while also being comfortable working independently. Assist with campus events, equipment moves, seasonal maintenance, and other Facilities needs as requested. Participate in emergency maintenance response, including occasional evenings, weekends, and holidays. Perform other duties as assigned. What We're Looking For Minimum Qualifications: At least 18 months of experience in the HVAC field . A combination of education, training, and/or experience that demonstrates the ability to successfully perform the essential duties may be considered in place of the minimum qualifications. Skills That Will Help You Succeed We're looking for someone with knowledge or experience in areas such as: HVAC and refrigeration systems and the refrigeration cycle Equipment and component identification Preventive maintenance and troubleshooting Electrical schematics and mechanical blueprints DX equipment and pneumatic components Motors, bearings, pumps, compressors, starters, and related mechanical components Soft soldering and repair of refrigerant, pneumatic, and water lines Workplace safety procedures and equipment Most importantly, you'll bring a strong work ethic, willingness to learn, reliability, and a commitment to working safely and as part of a team. Why Join OCU? At Oklahoma City University, you're joining more than a Facilities department. You're joining a team that believes in mentorship, teamwork, and helping employees build their careers. What you'll love about working here: Supportive, team-oriented work environment Hands-on experience with a variety of building systems On-the-job training and opportunities to expand your technical skills Stable employment and excellent benefits Employee tuition remission for eligible degrees and programs Educational benefits available to eligible spouses and dependents Opportunities to grow your career within Facilities and beyond The opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to a university community Build Your Career While Keeping Our Campus Moving Your work will have an impact every day—from keeping classrooms comfortable to ensuring essential equipment and building systems are working properly. Bring your skills. Learn something new. Be part of a team that invests in your future. Oklahoma City University is looking for two HVAC Maintenance Technicians ready to put their skills to work. Apply today and join our team! Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1e2f6d26 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Facilities Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 92bdbc1e Last Name (required) 55c6343e Email (required) 309def97 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director of Academic Achievement Law School Oklahoma City University School of Law seeks a Director of Academic Achievement, to begin on August 1, 2027.  This may be either a staff or faculty position, as described below. Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator Nursing School The Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Kramer School of Nursing and serves as the designated Nurse Administrator for purposes of ACEN accreditation and Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions, the Senior Associate Dean holds the authority and accountability required of the Nurse Administrator under Oklahoma Board of Nursing rules, including direct responsibility for administration of the School’s nursing education program, preparation and administration of the School budget, implementation of faculty development programs, and recommendation of qualified faculty for appointment, promotion, tenure (if applicable), and retention. The Senior Associate Dean ensures compliance and alignment with applicable accreditation and regulatory body standards and reporting requirements. As a senior member of college leadership, the Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator works collaboratively with the Dean in providing strategic and operational direction for the College. Program Director Law School OKLAHOMA CITY UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applications for the position of Program Director for the launch of its online J.D. program, which is currently being developed.   The online J.D. program will be fully online, and courses are likely to be both asynchronous and synchronous.  All online J.D. program faculty and staff will fulfill their responsibilities in person at OCU Law. Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing School The Kramer School of Nursing at Oklahoma City University invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure track Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing position. The successful candidate will begin as soon as possible. Recruitment Specialist Human Resources Oklahoma City University is seeking an organized, service-minded Recruitment Specialist to coordinate hiring across our campus community, from the first job posting to the new hire's first day. This role is ideal for an HR professional who thrives on process, is ready for ownership of a function, and understands that every search reflects the institution. Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist Facilities This position is responsible for the day-to-day maintenance operations of the HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and mechanical systems for the university. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4b38581c Last Name (required) a9e58f12 Email (required) 3fd82243 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Employment Opportunity Oklahoma City University pledges to recruit, select, and promote diversity by providing equality of opportunity in higher education for all current and prospective students, faculty, and staff with respect to hiring, continuation, promotion and tenure, and applications for admission or employment, without discrimination or segregation based on sex (gender), race, age, ancestry, color, disability, genetic history, national origin, marital status, medical condition, religious creed, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, pregnancy, parenting status, status as a veteran, or the perception that a person has one or more of these characteristics. For questions, concerns, and/or additional information, please contact: Applicants/Employees (ADA/Section 504) – Office of Human Resources: chamilton@okcu.edu / 405-208-6330 Title IX – Vice President for Student Affairs (Title IX Coordinator): aayres@okcu.edu / 405.208.7900 Titles VI and VII, Section 504 Title III, ADA and amendments, and ADEA – Chief Human Resources Officer: bbenson@okcu.edu / 405.208.6020 About Us | Contact Us Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Oklahoma City University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
