    "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-of-law-law-school-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states-f4591f09-c357-4529-a7ec-e85ae031b9bb": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Law",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Law - Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Home Jobs Mission/Values DEI Benefits Applicant Login Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate Professor of Law Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges 9 Month Faculty Opening at: Aug 4 2026 - 09:00 CDT Add to favorites View favorites VP Area: Law School Department: Law School FLSA Status: Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: OKLAHOMA CITY UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applications for 2-3 full-time, tenure-track faculty positions, to begin in Fall 2027. We welcome applications from candidates in all doctrinal areas, and we have particular needs in first-year courses (Civil Procedure, Contracts, Torts, Criminal Law, and Property). We seek applicants whose commitment to teaching, research, and service will enhance the learning of our students, broaden the impact of our faculty scholarship, and enrich our close-knit academic community. Candidates are expected to teach courses in both the in-person and the online J.D. program, which is currently being developed.  The online J.D. program will be fully online, and courses are likely to be both asynchronous and synchronous.  All full-time faculty will fulfill their responsibilities in person at OCU Law. In addition to 2-3 tenure-track faculty positions, OCU Law anticipates hiring a Legal Research & Writing Professor and a Program Director for the online J.D. program during the 2026-2027 hiring season, with successful candidates beginning appointments in fall 2027. Candidates should have an excellent academic background, a strong commitment to effective and engaged teaching, demonstrated potential to become a productive scholar, and a sincere commitment to integrity and a welcoming environment. We have built a community that values dedication, collegiality, and professionalism, and we are seeking candidates who share these values. Candidates must have either a J.D. degree from an ABA-accredited law school or the combination of a foreign law degree and either an L.L.M. or S.J.D. degree from a U.S. law school. Our beautiful, historic law building is in the heart of downtown Oklahoma City, the 21st-most-populous city in America. We are within walking distance of the federal and county courthouses, and we are deeply engaged with the legal, business, nonprofit, and government communities of the city and state. In fact, the Mayor of OKC (David Holt) is our OCU Law Dean. OKC is consistently ranked among America’s “Best Places to Live,” is home to the 2025 NBA Champion Thunder, and is hosting events in the 2028 Olympics. For more information about OKC, see https://www.visitokc.com . OCU Law is the home of the Oklahoma Innocence Project, the OCU Tribal Sovereignty Institute, and the USPTO’s Regional Pro Bono Patent Program. To apply, please submit a cover letter, CV, research agenda, and job-talk paper through the University’s hiring portal: https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/search . Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis.  No final hiring decisions can be made until candidates have applied through the portal.  For more information, contact the Chair of the Faculty Appointments Committee, Professor and Associate Dean Lee Peoples, at lpeoples@okcu.edu . Oklahoma City University is an equal opportunity employer and affirms the values and goals of diversity. See OCU Nondiscrimination Statement . Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 648be8fd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Law School Law School Locations Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Law School, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 593c3cdc Last Name (required) 749f650d Email (required) 22672f52 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director of Academic Achievement Law School Oklahoma City University School of Law seeks a Director of Academic Achievement, to begin on August 1, 2027.  This may be either a staff or faculty position, as described below. Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator Nursing School The Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Kramer School of Nursing and serves as the designated Nurse Administrator for purposes of ACEN accreditation and Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions, the Senior Associate Dean holds the authority and accountability required of the Nurse Administrator under Oklahoma Board of Nursing rules, including direct responsibility for administration of the School’s nursing education program, preparation and administration of the School budget, implementation of faculty development programs, and recommendation of qualified faculty for appointment, promotion, tenure (if applicable), and retention. The Senior Associate Dean ensures compliance and alignment with applicable accreditation and regulatory body standards and reporting requirements. As a senior member of college leadership, the Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator works collaboratively with the Dean in providing strategic and operational direction for the College. Program Director Law School OKLAHOMA CITY UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applications for the position of Program Director for the launch of its online J.D. program, which is currently being developed.   The online J.D. program will be fully online, and courses are likely to be both asynchronous and synchronous.  All online J.D. program faculty and staff will fulfill their responsibilities in person at OCU Law. Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing School The Kramer School of Nursing at Oklahoma City University invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure track Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing position. The successful candidate will begin as soon as possible. Recruitment Specialist Human Resources Oklahoma City University is seeking an organized, service-minded Recruitment Specialist to coordinate hiring across our campus community, from the first job posting to the new hire's first day. This role is ideal for an HR professional who thrives on process, is ready for ownership of a function, and understands that every search reflects the institution. Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist Facilities This position is responsible for the day-to-day maintenance operations of the HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and mechanical systems for the university. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 7957c345 Last Name (required) 12f7b436 Email (required) da3c8b70 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Employment Opportunity Oklahoma City University pledges to recruit, select, and promote diversity by providing equality of opportunity in higher education for all current and prospective students, faculty, and staff with respect to hiring, continuation, promotion and tenure, and applications for admission or employment, without discrimination or segregation based on sex (gender), race, age, ancestry, color, disability, genetic history, national origin, marital status, medical condition, religious creed, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, pregnancy, parenting status, status as a veteran, or the perception that a person has one or more of these characteristics. For questions, concerns, and/or additional information, please contact: Applicants/Employees (ADA/Section 504) – Office of Human Resources: chamilton@okcu.edu / 405-208-6330 Title IX – Vice President for Student Affairs (Title IX Coordinator): aayres@okcu.edu / 405.208.7900 Titles VI and VII, Section 504 Title III, ADA and amendments, and ADEA – Chief Human Resources Officer: bbenson@okcu.edu / 405.208.6020 About Us | Contact Us Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Oklahoma City University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
