    "https://careers.okcu.edu/jobs/advanced-practice-clinical-liaison-main-campus-oklahoma-city-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Clinical Liaison",
      "description": "Advanced Practice Clinical Liaison - Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Home Jobs Mission/Values DEI Benefits Applicant Login Kiosk mode Advanced Practice Clinical Liaison Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Schools and Colleges Regular Full-Time Staff Opening at: Apr 17 2026 - 09:00 CDT Add to favorites View favorites VP Area: Nursing School Department: Nursing School FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: Department: Nursing School FLSA Status: Non-Exempt Benefit Eligibility: Yes Position Summary: About the Role: Oklahoma City University is seeking a relationship-driven professional to help grow clinical placement opportunities for the Kramer School of Nursing's Advanced Practice Programs. This role offers the opportunity to build lasting partnerships with hospitals, clinics, and healthcare organizations across the region while directly supporting the education of the next generation of advanced practice nurses. As Advanced Practice Clinical Liaison, you'll be a member of the Kramer School of Nursing team, partnering closely with the Operations Manager and program faculty to identify, recruit, and maintain the clinical sites and preceptors that make hands-on learning possible. This position is well suited for an organized professional with strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills, who is comfortable representing the university to outside partners, and takes real satisfaction in helping students succeed. The Liaison reports to the Operations Manager and works closely with faculty throughout the Kramer School of Nursing. What You'll Do: As Advanced Practice Clinical Liaison, you'll identify and cultivate clinical site and affiliation opportunities, and serve as the primary point of contact for students, faculty, and external partners throughout the placement process. Key responsibilities include: Identifying and cultivating new clinical site and affiliation opportunities to support program growth and student learning needs Developing and maintaining positive relationships with clinical sites, agencies, and healthcare partners Identifying, recruiting, and retaining qualified preceptors Conducting site visits and evaluations of potential preceptors and facilities using standardized criteria Working with the Graduate Specialist to maintain clinical site affiliation agreements and required compliance paperwork Serving as the primary staff touchstone for graduate students throughout the clinical placement process Advising students on clinical assignments and troubleshooting placement and scheduling issues as they arise Maintaining accurate records and generating reports on placement activities Representing the Kramer School of Nursing at recruitment and community events, with some regional travel and occasional evening or weekend commitments What We're Looking For: Successful candidates will bring strong interpersonal skills, sound judgment, and an interest in healthcare education. Preferred qualifications include: Two or more years of experience in administrative coordination, project coordination, higher education, healthcare, or a related professional setting preferred. Recent graduates with relevant internship, practicum, or coursework are also encouraged to apply. Demonstrated success building and maintaining professional relationships Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills Highly organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable managing multiple priorities at once Ability to manage day-to-day work with general guidance while collaborating effectively across departments Professional judgment and discretion in handling confidential information Willingness for some regional travel and to participate in occasional evening and weekend events Comfort with Microsoft Office Suite and willingness to learn new university software and systems A bachelor's degree is preferred; an equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered in lieu of the degree Why Oklahoma City University: At OCU, you'll find meaningful work, supportive colleagues, and a benefits package designed to support you and your family throughout your career. Highlights include: Medical, dental, and vision insurance with significant university premium contributions University-paid life and long-term disability insurance Retirement plan with university matching contributions up to 5% Generous paid time off and 16.5 paid holidays annually Summer hours schedule with offices closed on Fridays during the summer Tuition remission opportunities for employees and eligible dependents attending OCU Participation in Tuition Exchange and CIC Tuition Exchange programs, providing eligible dependent children access to scholarship opportunities at participating institutions nationwide Flexible spending and health savings account options Employee assistance and wellness resources Professional development opportunities Located in the heart of Oklahoma City, OCU combines the energy of a thriving metropolitan area with the close-knit culture of a university community where individual contributions are valued and recognized. Apply Now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert dcdf8326 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Nursing School Nursing School Locations Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States Main Campus, Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States First Name (required) 8d115c4d Last Name (required) 7a7af12e Email (required) 015bb987 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Director of Academic Achievement Law School Oklahoma City University School of Law seeks a Director of Academic Achievement, to begin on August 1, 2027.  This may be either a staff or faculty position, as described below. Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator Nursing School The Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator provides academic and administrative leadership for the Kramer School of Nursing and serves as the designated Nurse Administrator for purposes of ACEN accreditation and Oklahoma Board of Nursing program approval. Reporting directly to the Dean of the College of Nursing and Health Professions, the Senior Associate Dean holds the authority and accountability required of the Nurse Administrator under Oklahoma Board of Nursing rules, including direct responsibility for administration of the School’s nursing education program, preparation and administration of the School budget, implementation of faculty development programs, and recommendation of qualified faculty for appointment, promotion, tenure (if applicable), and retention. The Senior Associate Dean ensures compliance and alignment with applicable accreditation and regulatory body standards and reporting requirements. As a senior member of college leadership, the Senior Associate Dean and Nurse Administrator works collaboratively with the Dean in providing strategic and operational direction for the College. Program Director Law School OKLAHOMA CITY UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applications for the position of Program Director for the launch of its online J.D. program, which is currently being developed.   The online J.D. program will be fully online, and courses are likely to be both asynchronous and synchronous.  All online J.D. program faculty and staff will fulfill their responsibilities in person at OCU Law. Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing Nursing School The Kramer School of Nursing at Oklahoma City University invites applications for a 12-month, non-tenure track Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor of Nursing position. The successful candidate will begin as soon as possible. Recruitment Specialist Human Resources Oklahoma City University is seeking an organized, service-minded Recruitment Specialist to coordinate hiring across our campus community, from the first job posting to the new hire's first day. This role is ideal for an HR professional who thrives on process, is ready for ownership of a function, and understands that every search reflects the institution. Preventative Maintenance Program Specialist Facilities This position is responsible for the day-to-day maintenance operations of the HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and mechanical systems for the university. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 09609320 Last Name (required) 3df54567 Email (required) 4b1a2c12 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Employment Opportunity Oklahoma City University pledges to recruit, select, and promote diversity by providing equality of opportunity in higher education for all current and prospective students, faculty, and staff with respect to hiring, continuation, promotion and tenure, and applications for admission or employment, without discrimination or segregation based on sex (gender), race, age, ancestry, color, disability, genetic history, national origin, marital status, medical condition, religious creed, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, pregnancy, parenting status, status as a veteran, or the perception that a person has one or more of these characteristics. For questions, concerns, and/or additional information, please contact: Applicants/Employees (ADA/Section 504) – Office of Human Resources: chamilton@okcu.edu / 405-208-6330 Title IX – Vice President for Student Affairs (Title IX Coordinator): aayres@okcu.edu / 405.208.7900 Titles VI and VII, Section 504 Title III, ADA and amendments, and ADEA – Chief Human Resources Officer: bbenson@okcu.edu / 405.208.6020 About Us | Contact Us Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Oklahoma City University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, 